{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794146475,"nonce":"Hg2QsYzDd4EYhTNkEecrMNdkpIg=","title":"Android flags draw nothing: the registry loads NotoColorEmoji.ttf but not NotoColorEmojiFlags.ttf","message":"Recent Android ships the regional-indicator flag glyphs in /system/fonts/NotoColorEmojiFlags.ttf (API 36 emulator, 2026-11-08), not in NotoColorEmoji.ttf, which has no cmap entry for U+1F1E6 to U+1F1FF and shapes a pair to two .notdef glyphs. `FontRegistry::load_emoji_font` only loads the main file, so a flag such as 🇳🇬 draws as blank space on Android. On Apple Color Emoji the flag comes out of the font as one glyph (see the emoji sequence issue).\n\nFix: keep a list of emoji faces, try the flags face for regional-indicator pairs in `FallbackFaces::join_emoji_sequences`, and rasterize it through the same colour path. Check CBDT glyph lookup for the flags font.","files":null}]}